Description: pvr: bound the idle render states by size as well
 The render state cache for dynamic rendering keeps up to 16 render states
 without references. Each of them holds its SPM scratch buffer, which scales
 with width, height, sample count, output registers and tile buffers
 (pvr_arch_spm_scratch_buffer_calc_required_size()), and the render target
 dataset of its first job, whose buffers grow with the number of tiles and
 layers. The scratch buffer store only shares a buffer
 between render states of exactly the size of the last one, so render states
 of different sizes each hold their own. At 1920x1080 with one sample and one
 output register a scratch buffer is about 8 MiB, at 3840x2160 about 32 MiB,
 and with 4 samples at 3840x2160 about 127 MiB; 16 idle render states can then
 hold several hundred MiB to about 2 GiB, for example after a window was
 resized through many sizes.
 .
 Count the scratch buffer sizes of the idle render states and evict the
 least recently used ones while the sum exceeds 64 MiB, in addition to the
 limit of 16 entries. The most recently used idle render state is always kept,
 so a single large render target still gets the cached render state. The
 datasets are not counted. Evicted render states are taken off the idle list
 under the cache lock and destroyed after it is released; render states with
 references are never on the idle list and are not touched.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
